      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the first six prime numbers.\n2. Calculate the sum of the first five prime numbers.\n3. Find the remainder when this sum is divided by the sixth prime number.\n\nLet's start with step 1: identifying the first six prime numbers.\n\nThe first six prime numbers are:\n\\[ 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13 \\]\n\nNext, we move to step 2: calculating the sum of the first five prime numbers.\n\nThe first five prime numbers are:\n\\[ 2, 3, 5, 7, 11 \\]\n\nWe sum these numbers:\n\\[\n2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11\n\\]\n\nCalculating the sum step-by-step:\n\\[\n2 + 3 = 5\n\\]\n\\[\n5 + 5 = 10\n\\]\n\\[\n10 + 7 = 17\n\\]\n\\[\n17 + 11 = 28\n\\]\n\nSo, the sum of the first five prime numbers is:\n\\[\n28\n\\]\n\nNow, we move to step 3: finding the remainder when this sum is divided by the sixth prime number.\n\nThe sixth prime number is:\n\\[ 13 \\]\n\nWe need to find the remainder when 28 is divided by 13. We perform the division:\n\\[\n28 \\div 13 = 2 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 28 - (2 \\times 13) = 28 - 26 = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the remainder when 28 is divided by 13 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
