      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the first six prime numbers.**\n   \n   The first six prime numbers are:\n   \\[\n   2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the sum of the first five primes.**\n\n   The first five primes are:\n   \\[\n   2, 3, 5, 7, 11\n   \\]\n\n   Adding these together:\n   \\[\n   2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11\n   \\]\n\n   Let's perform the addition step by step:\n   \\[\n   2 + 3 = 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   5 + 5 = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   10 + 7 = 17\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   17 + 11 = 28\n   \\]\n\n   So, the sum of the first five primes is:\n   \\[\n   28\n   \\]\n\n3. **Identify the sixth prime number.**\n\n   The sixth prime number is:\n   \\[\n   13\n   \\]\n\n4. **Divide the sum by the sixth prime and find the remainder.**\n\n   We need to find the remainder when 28 is divided by 13. We perform the division:\n   \\[\n   28 \\div 13 \\approx 2.1538\n   \\]\n\n   The integer part of the quotient is 2. To find the remainder, we calculate:\n   \\[\n   28 - (13 \\times 2) = 28 - 26 = 2\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, the remainder when 28 is divided by 13 is:\n   \\[\n   2\n   \\]\n\n5. **Present the final answer.**\n\n   The remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{2}\n   \\]",
